# Implementation routing

Do not infer current project status from historical phase documents or Git history.

Start from:

- `IMPLEMENTATION.md` — repository implementation entry point;
- `docs/implementation/README.md` — sole living implementation-program status authority;
- `docs/implementation/agent_reference_index.md` — compact domain-to-contract/document lookup;
- `docs/implementation/AGENTS.md` — implementation engineering discipline;
- the active implementation package/group plan;
- `docs/concepts/phase_010/09_architecture_consolidation_validation_exit/implementation_handoff.md` — frozen architecture handoff.

Current program entry is **Implementation 001 — Executable Foundations & Walking Skeleton** until `docs/implementation/README.md` says otherwise.

Rules:

- read only the active package/group plus domain-specific references needed for the task;
- search stable contract IDs (`REF-###`, `AUTH-###`, `HLTH-###`, `OPS-###`, `EXPL-###`, `INTG-###`, `ARCH-###`) instead of loading whole phases;
- code/tests/schemas/Databricks resources/CI are permitted within active implementation scope;
- implementation convenience never supersedes accepted contracts;
- design-scenario PASS is not executable implementation proof.
